<body>
    <h1>AI-244: Facial Recognition Frame Accuracy Fix Configuration and Usa=
ge</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>This guide explains how to configure frame processing for facial=
 recognition tasks. The workflow involves two main steps:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Initial Frame Sampling</strong>: Frames are sampled based on a p=
redefined rate (e.g., <code>frame_sampling_per_minute</code>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Adjacent Frame Sampling</strong>: For each frame where a face is=
 detected, additional frames are sampled based on the <code>time_offset</co=
de> and <code>offset_direction</code> configurations.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>This process continues until no more faces are detected in the sampled f=
rames or the frames have already been processed.</p>
<h2 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-Key=
ConfigurationOptions">Key Configuration Options</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-1.t=
ime_offset">1. time_offset</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-Wha=
titdoes:">What it does:</h4>
<p>This setting defines the time interval (in milliseconds) used to determi=
ne how far to look in the specified <code>offset_direction</code> for adjac=
ent frames.</p>
<h4 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-How=
itworks:">How it works:</h4>
<p>After a face is detected in a frame, the system uses <code>time_offset</=
code> to calculate how many frames to skip before sampling the next frame.<=
/p>
<p>The number of frames to offset is calculated as:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">frame_o=
ffset =3D int(frame_rate * (time_offset / 1000))</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>For example, if <code>time_offset =3D 1000 ms</code> and <code>frame_rat=
e =3D 30 fps</code>, the offset is 30 frames.</p>
<h4 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-Whe=
ntouseit:">When to use it:</h4>
<p>Use this to control how far apart the sampled frames should be when look=
ing for adjacent frames.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-2.o=
ffset_direction">2. offset_direction</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-Wha=
titdoes:.1">What it does:</h4>
<p>This setting determines the direction in which to sample adjacent frames=
 relative to the current frame.</p>
<h4 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-Opt=
ions:">Options:</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>"forward"</strong>: Only sample frames after the current frame.<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>"backward"</strong>: Only sample frames before the current frame=
.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>"both"</strong>: Sample frames both before and after the current=
 frame.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>"none"</strong>: Do not sample adjacent frames.</p></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-How=
itworks:.1">How it works:</h4>
<p>Once a face is detected in a frame, the system uses <code>offset_directi=
on</code> to decide whether to look forward, backward, both, or not at all.=
</p>
<p>The <code>time_offset</code> value determines how far to look in the cho=
sen direction(s).</p>
<p><strong>Example:</strong> If <code>time_offset =3D 1000 ms</code>, <code=
>frame_rate =3D 30 fps</code>, and <code>offset_direction =3D "forward"</co=
de>, the system will sample the frame 30 frames after the current one.</p>
<h4 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-Whe=
ntouseit:.1">When to use it:</h4>
<p>Use this to control the direction in which to search for adjacent frames=
 after a face is detected.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-3.m=
ax_interval">3. max_interval</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-Wha=
titdoes:.2">What it does:</h4>
<p>This setting defines the maximum time difference (in milliseconds) betwe=
en two consecutive frames where a face exists, to consider the face in rang=
e (still visible in the shot).</p>
<h4 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-How=
itworks:.2">How it works:</h4>
<p>After all frames are processed and the results are gathered (all frames =
containing the face we want), a range is built where that face exists in th=
e video. If the time difference between two consecutive frames where the fa=
ce is detected is greater than <code>max_interval</code>, the system consid=
ers it as a new appearance of the face.</p>
<p><strong>Example:</strong> If <code>max_interval =3D 1000 ms</code>, and =
two frames where the face is detected are 1200 ms apart, they will be treat=
ed as separate occurrences of the face.</p>
<h4 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-Whe=
ntouseit:.2">When to use it:</h4>
<p>Use this to control how long a face can be missing from consecutive fram=
es before considering it to have disappeared.</p>
<h2 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-Exa=
mpleConfiguration">Example Configuration</h2>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s how you can set up and use these configurations in your w=
orkflow:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
  "backedn":"retinaface",
  "identification_threshold":0.75,
  "frame_sampling_per_minute":30,
  "processing":{
    "time_offset":1000, # default
    "offset_direction":"forward", # default
    "max_interval":1000 # default
  }
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"AI-244:FacialRecognitionFrameAccuracyFixConfigurationandUsage-Sum=
mary">Summary</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>time_offset</strong>: Determines how far to look in the specifie=
d direction for adjacent frames.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>offset_direction</strong>: Controls the direction (forward, back=
ward, both, or none) to sample adjacent frames.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>max_interval</strong>: Defines the maximum time difference betwe=
en two consecutive frames where a face exists to consider it in range.</p><=
/li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
